# Charts with VegaLite

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:kino_vega_lite, "~> 0.1.13"},
  {:req, "~> 0.7"}
])

alias VegaLite, as: Vl
```

## Fetching the data

This notebook downloads the Gapminder dataset with Req and plots the countries' fertility against their life expectancy in 2005 with VegaLite. In the browser, Req downloads with `fetch()`, so it only works with servers that allow cross-origin requests, like jsDelivr's mirror of npm packages.

```elixir
countries =
  Req.get!("https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-datasets@2/data/gapminder.json").body
  |> Enum.filter(&(&1["year"] == 2005))

length(countries)
```

## Plotting it

Hover over a point to see its country.

```elixir
Vl.new(width: 600, height: 400, title: "Fertility and life expectancy in 2005")
|> Vl.data_from_values(countries)
|> Vl.mark(:circle, opacity: 0.8)
|> Vl.encode_field(:x, "fertility", type: :quantitative, title: "Children per woman")
|> Vl.encode_field(:y, "life_expect",
  type: :quantitative,
  title: "Life expectancy",
  scale: [zero: false]
)
|> Vl.encode_field(:size, "pop",
  type: :quantitative,
  title: "Population",
  scale: [range: [25, 1500]]
)
|> Vl.encode_field(:color, "cluster", type: :nominal, legend: nil)
|> Vl.encode_field(:tooltip, "country", type: :nominal)
```
